  "observed_source": [
    "rSa derives both terminal disableStdin and nZe disableInput from whether the task process is running.",
    "nZe attaches the live runtime session using tIr/Loi; tIr.onInput subscribes terminal.onData and applies the dynamic disableInput gate.",
    "Runtime attachRenderer uses MSt/TSt input scheduling; spawnBackendSession enables input after readiness and disables it on exit. Runtime.write checks running and isInputEnabled before backendSession.write.",
    "Shared qc import resolves to ts via gh. Default runtime factory DAt uses FAt; its local backend _St creates ySt, whose write method invokes pty_write.",
    "Current ScriptsPanel supplies ScriptOutput with output only. ScriptOutput constructs xterm with disableStdin:true and no onData subscription.",
    "Current scripts API/Tauri command declarations expose run start/stop/status/output but no write-input route.",
    "Current launch::spawn gives the PTY master File to the reader thread; Process retains no writer. RunManager tracks the live Process by workspace/script and retains only transcript output after exit."
  ],
  "conclusion": "The checked current running-script path lacks the reference input route. A frontend-only enablement cannot reach the checked script Process. This is a source discrepancy, not a reproduced native failure.",
